<title>USA: USDA sets special import quota for cotton.</title>
<headline>USDA sets special import quota for cotton.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>High cotton prices have triggered another special import quota that will allow imports of 44.3 million kilograms, the Agriculture Department said Thursday.</p>
<p>The quota will be established on June 12, and will be applied to upland cotton purchased no later than Sept. 9 and imported no later than Dec. 8, the USDA said.</p>
<p>The USDA can establish a special import quota if for any consecutive 10-week period, the U.S. Northern Europe price exceeds the Northern Europe price by more than 1.25 cents per pound.</p>
</text>
